 "notes": [
  "Employment-based Form I-485 petitions are generally adjudicated by USCIS’ Field Office Directorate. To find processing times for employment-based Forms I-485 in the first (EB-1), second (EB-2), and third (EB-3) preference categories, use the filters for field office locations. The processing times listed for Service Center Operations are only for fourth preference (EB-4) and fifth preference (EB-5) Form I-485 employment-based cases. The processing times shown on the website do not include visa-regressed adjustment applications. If an applicant's priority date is not earlier than the applicable visa available cut-off date published in the Visa Bulletin (available at travel.state.gov), we cannot approve their adjustment of status application until a visa is available to them based on their priority date, preference category, and country of chargeability.",
  "The Service Center Operations Directorate no longer receives Form I-485 applications based on a grant of asylum status. As of Sept. 28, 2020, the Field Operations Directorate receives all Form I-485 applications based on a grant of asylum status. If you have a case filed before that time that a service center is working on, you may ask for more information through the USCIS eRequest Service Tool online (egov.uscis.gov/e-request/Intro.do) or by calling the USCIS Contact Center.",
  "The Service Center Operations Directorate no longer receives Form I-485 applications based on a grant of refugee status. As of Sept. 28, 2020, the Field Operations Directorate receives all Form I-485 applications based on a grant of refugee status. If you have a case filed before that time that a service center is working on, you may ask for more information through the USCIS eRequest Service Tool online (egov.uscis.gov/e-request/Intro.do) or by calling the USCIS Contact Center.",
  "***Note: This calculation for the National Benefits Center’s processing time is specifically for adoption-based Form I-130s. The National Benefits Center adjudicates all adoption-based Form I-130s.***This processing time reflects statutory constraints on available immigrant visas, for which the wait times are typically much longer than the time it takes for USCIS to adjudicate the form.***USCIS service centers prioritize the processing of Form I-130 preference petitions for which an immigrant visa is available according to the Department of State Visa Bulletin. The visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. We use the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing Form I-130 preference petitions. We are prioritizing our adjudication efforts to focus on cases that have visas available.",
  "***This processing time reflects statutory constraints on available immigrant visas, for which the wait times are typically much longer than the time it takes for USCIS to adjudicate the form.***USCIS service centers prioritize the processing of Form I-130 preference petitions for which an immigrant visa is available according to the Department of State Visa Bulletin. The visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. We use the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing Form I-130 preference petitions. We are prioritizing our adjudication efforts to focus on cases that have visas available.",
  "***Note: This calculation for the National Benefits Center’s processing time is specifically for adoption-based Form I-130s. The National Benefits Center adjudicates all adoption-based Form I-130s.*** The Department of State visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. USCIS uses the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing a Form I-130 preference petition.",
  "USCIS service centers are now prioritizing the processing of Form I-130 preference petitions for which the Department of State Visa Bulletin shows that an immigrant visa is available. The visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. USCIS uses the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing a Form I-130 preference petition. Service centers have prioritized our adjudication efforts so that we can focus on those cases that have visas available.",
  "USCIS posts 1 processing time for any service center location that processes requests for an Employment Authorization Document based on a pending asylum application. We keep these requests in an electronic system that allows us generally to process adjudication-ready cases in the order USCIS receives them, regardless of where the case is pending or where the adjudicator is.",
  "USCIS posts 1 processing time for any service center location that processes requests for an initial Employment Authorization Document based on a pending asylum application. We keep these requests in an electronic system that allows us generally to process adjudication-ready cases in the order USCIS receives them, regardless of where the case is pending or where the adjudicator is.",
  "USCIS Service Center Operations (SCOPS) prioritizes processing of Form I-140, Immigrant Petition for Alien Workers, when the Department of State Visa Bulletin shows an immigrant visa is available. The Visa Bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. We use the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates. SCOPS has prioritized our adjudications so we can focus on cases with visas available and can move related Applications to Register Permanent Residence or Adjust Status (Form I-485) to the National Benefits Center. This prioritization supports the USCIS-wide effort to use all employment-based visas available during the fiscal year. It does not affect premium processed petitions, which we will manage in the associated time frame for premium processing service.",
  "Processing time represents the number of elapsed days between the received date and the first adjudicative decision, which may include RFE response days. We do not include reopened cases.",
  "Processing time represents the number of elapsed days between the received date and the first adjudicative decision, which may include RFE response days. We do not include reopened cases. *** If you are a petitioner for an H-2A Temporary Agricultural Worker and your Form I-129 has been pending longer than 15 days and you have not received a decision or a Request for Evidence, you may contact USCIS at (1-800) 375-5283 to inquire about your petition.",
  "Since October 2025, H-2A petitioners seeking unnamed beneficiaries can electronically file an H-2A petition with USCIS after the U.S. Department of Labor (DOL) issues a notice of acceptance of the application for temporary labor certification (TLC) and before DOL approves a TLC. However, USCIS will not approve these petitions until after DOL has approved the corresponding TLC. This concurrent processing has contributed to longer H-2A petition processing times because USCIS must now wait until DOL approves the corresponding TLC before we can process the H-2A petition."
 ],
